Ques1. What is asynchronous JavaScript?
Ans:- Asynchronous JavaScript allows a program to start a task and continue executing other code without waiting for that task to finish.

Ques2:-JavaScript is synchronous or asynchrous ?
Ans:- It is Synchronous and single threaded But Synchronous and Single Threaded  is default javaScript Behaviour 

Ques3. What is synchronous JavaScript?
Answer: Synchronous JavaScript executes code one statement at a time, in order. Each operation must finish before the next operation starts.

blocking code:- block the flow of program => read file sync
Non blocking:- does not block excution  => read file async

